# Day 23/50 — TCP vs UDP

Not all data needs to travel in the same way.

Imagine sending an important document
You would want to make sure every page reaches the receiver correctly.

Now imagine watching a live video, waiting for every missing frame might ruin the experience.

That's the difference between two common transport protocols.

**TCP** focuses on reliable, ordered delivery, it checks that data reaches its destination correctly.

**UDP** is faster and connectionless, but doesn't guarantee delivery or order.

Neither is universally better. 
The right choice depends on what the application needs.

It's a reminder that speed and reliability aren't always the same thing.

**Sometimes, the best way forward depends on what matters more in that moment**
